# Built output is committed: the harness loads `lib/`, and a deploy must be
# reproducible from a clean checkout without a build toolchain.
!lib/

# The runtime scope junction that makes bare `@deepseek-ai/*` resolve from this
# repo. It is machine-specific, so it must never be committed.
node_modules/

# Upstream pstack prose is re-synced, never edited here, so a local edit to a
# mirrored skill is almost always a mistake. This used to be enforced by keeping
# skills/ out of git — but the harness loads skills from `<plugin>/skills`, so a
# clone with no skills/ installs a plugin that answers nothing. It is committed
# instead, and `tests/seam.test.mjs` enforces the same rule the hard way: it
# re-syncs from upstream and fails if the committed tree differs by one byte.
# A hand edit now fails a test rather than being uncommittable.

# Local scratch and backups.
*.bak
lib.backup-*/

# A local copy of the upstream pstack tree, used by the seam test. Third-party
# prose, not our work, and not needed to use the plugin — never committed.
upstream/
